  "_comment": "T342: both peers fly Taurus and press LUNGE twice (ticks 150/180 and 600/640, past the 5.5 s cooldown) while walking and turning. The client's own lunge is predicted from the input tick the server ran it on (_rpc_lunge): prediction_recon must stay in its usual bounds (a lunge started a round trip late would put the owner ~1 m off = a snap); the server's copy and the client's view must agree (transform_desync); any ram damage must replicate (health_desync). Own link: 160 ms each way (320 ms round trip, longer than the 0.2 s windup), so the owner's catch-up (_rpc_lunge rewrites the ticks it ran past the server's start) is what keeps it in bounds; on wifi / bad the windup alone hides the delay. Snaps capped at 1%: without the catch-up the client's lunge peaked at 1.16 m with 2 snaps of 187 (a rubber-band; the run's p95 still passed), with it 0.02 m, none; B131: on a lossy link (sweep @bad) a lost start RPC can still cost one snap, then the snapshot's lunge clock takes over.",
